    {
      "number": 1,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:1",
      "text": "So copy God's way, like the kids he loves."
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:2",
      "text": "Live in love, the way Christ loved us and gave himself for us—a gift and sacrifice to God, like a beautiful fragrance. 💛"
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:3",
      "text": "Sexual sin, every kind of impurity, and greed shouldn't even get a shout-out among you; God's people should know better."
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:4",
      "text": "Drop the dirty talk, foolish chatter, and crude jokes—they don't fit. Let your words be thankful instead."
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:5",
      "text": "Know this for sure: people who live in sexual sin, impurity, or greed (which is idolatry) have no inheritance in Christ's and God's Kingdom."
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:6",
      "text": "Don't let anyone sell you empty talk. These things bring God's anger on people who disobey."
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:7",
      "text": "So don't join in with them."
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:8",
      "text": "You used to be darkness; now you're light in the Lord. Live like children of light. ✨"
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:9",
      "text": "The fruit of the light shows up in all goodness, right living, and truth."
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:10",
      "text": "Keep checking what makes the Lord glad."
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:11",
      "text": "Don't join the fruitless works of darkness; bring them into the light instead."
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:12",
      "text": "It's shameful even to talk about the secret things they do."
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
   …342 tokens truncated…t."
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:21",
      "text": "Out of respect for Christ, put each other first."
    },
    {
      "number": 22,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:22",
      "text": "Wives, be subject to your own husbands, as you are to the Lord."
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:23",
      "text": "The husband is the head of the wife, just as Christ is the head of the church—and Christ is the Savior of his body."
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:24",
      "text": "Just as the church is subject to Christ, wives should be subject to their own husbands in everything."
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:25",
      "text": "Husbands, love your wives the way Christ loved the church and gave himself up for her—"
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:26",
      "text": "to make her holy, cleansing her with the washing of water through the word,"
    },
    {
      "number": 27,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:27",
      "text": "so he could present the church to himself in glory, with no stain, wrinkle, or anything like that—holy and blameless."
    },
    {
      "number": 28,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:28",
      "text": "In the same way, husbands should love their wives as their own bodies. The man who loves his wife loves himself."
    },
    {
      "number": 29,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:29",
      "text": "No one ever hated their own body; they feed it and care for it, just as the Lord cares for the church—"
    },
    {
      "number": 30,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:30",
      "text": "because we are parts of his body, of his flesh and bones."
    },
    {
      "number": 31,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:31",
      "text": "Scripture says, ‘That's why a man leaves his father and mother, joins his wife, and the two become one.’"
    },
    {
      "number": 32,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:32",
      "text": "This mystery is profound—but I'm talking about Christ and the church."
    },
    {
      "number": 33,
      "sourceRef": "eng-web:EPH:5:33",
      "text": "Still, each husband must love his wife as himself, and each wife must respect her husband. 💍"
    }
